From: Darius Mercadier <dmercadier@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 12:57:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [Backport] CVE-2026-79197: Use after free in V8 (1/4)

Manual cherry-pick of patch originally reviewed on
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8131283:
[debug] Deoptimize topmost optimized frame on debugger break

When the debugger pauses, it can execute arbitrary JS (e.g. via
evaluation or inspector listeners). This JS can modify heap state,
such as detaching ArrayBuffers.

If the execution stack contains optimized frames, they might be using
load-eliminated values (like backing store pointers or array lengths)
that are now invalidated by the heap modifications.

To prevent use-after-free or out-of-bounds accesses when resuming,
deoptimize the topmost optimized JS frame when handling a debug break.
We only need to deoptimize the topmost frame because any caller frames
are at a call site, which acts as a memory serialization barrier,
forcing them to reload all heap state upon return anyway.

